  "id": "COMPOUND:307 - PROTEIN:1644",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests that gefitinib may interact with Tyrosine-protein kinase Lck through multiple indirect pathways. The first path links gefitinib to Ephrin type-A receptor 6, which is then targeted by a compound ([(2R,3S,4R,5R,6R)-6-[...]-yl]methyl acetate), which in turn targets Tyrosine-protein kinase Lck. The second path connects gefitinib to Ephrin type-A receptor 6, which is also targeted by Sinocalycanchinensin G, which directly targets Tyrosine-protein kinase Lck. The third path shows that gefitinib targets Serine/threonine-protein kinase TAO1, which is targeted by methohexital, which also targets Tyrosine-protein kinase Lck. These findings collectively suggest that gefitinib may influence Tyrosine-protein kinase Lck through different molecular mechanisms, possibly by modulating the activity of downstream targets that are themselves targets of other compounds. The integration of these pathways highlights the complexity of the relationship between gefitinib and Tyrosine-protein kinase Lck, emphasizing the role of receptor-targeting compounds in mediating this interaction.",
